
## Work tracking (break-free-github-flow)
In a session launched by Firstmate (a `FIRSTMATE_OP` launch brief) or run from a Firstmate home, skip this section: Firstmate owns dispatch, task tracking, worktrees and review there.
Every engineering task in a GitHub repository — bug, feature, refactor, debugging, CI or deployment change — is tracked in a GitHub issue: find or create it before changing code, keep it updated at milestones, and close it out with what changed, how it was verified (real results), and CI/deployment state. After any push, merge or deploy, watch the resulting workflow run and, if it fails, troubleshoot to root cause instead of re-running. Use the `break-free-github-flow` skill (`$break-free-github-flow`). Skip only if `gh` is not authenticated or the user says the work is throwaway.
